        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Schuyler, H. G. Wells, Darragh Park\n- Works: The Time Machine, The Island of Doctor Moreau, The Invisible Man, The War of the Worlds, The Morning of the Poem\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize for Poetry\n- Roles: artist, literary executor\n\nFacts:\n- H. G. Wells's notable science fiction works include The Time Machine (1895), The Island of Doctor Moreau (1896), The Invisible Man (1897), and The War of the Worlds (1898).\n- James Schuyler won the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry for his 1980 collection The Morning of the Poem.\n- Darragh Park was born on July 24, 1939, and died on April 17, 2009.\n- Darragh Park was an American artist and the literary executor of the estate of Pulitzer Prize-winning poet James Schuyler.",
